{"format":1,"key":"zone:hinterlands","path":"/lore/zone/hinterlands","name":"The Hinterlands","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"hinterlands","name":"The Hinterlands","path":"/lore/zone/hinterlands"},"levels":"","description":"The Hinterlands are a rugged, densely forested wilderness in eastern Lordaeron, tucked between the Plaguelands and the sea. The region is defined by…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:hinterlands","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["The Hinterlands are a rugged, densely forested wilderness in eastern Lordaeron, tucked between the Plaguelands and the sea. The region is defined by ancient Amani troll temple ruins, the towering aeries of the Wildhammer clan at Aerie Peak, and a colossal Great Tree anchoring a mysterious rift to the Emerald Dream.","Long before humans or dwarves walked northern Lordaeron, the forest trolls of the Amani Empire held dominion over the Hinterlands. Following their defeat in the ancient Troll Wars, their empire shattered into disparate tribes. Centuries later, after the tragic War of the Three Hammers drove the Wildhammer dwarves from Grim Batol, the dwarves migrated north and made their home on the surface at Aerie Peak. Taming the native gryphons and embracing shamanic traditions, the Wildhammer constructed a massive skybound stronghold. The trolls viewed these surface-dwelling dwarves as unwelcome squatters upon ancestral lands, sparking a ceaseless feud of skirmishes and raids.","Three distinct forest troll factions occupy the dense canopy and crumbling stone temples. The brutal and fanatical Vilebranch tribe is the strongest, maintaining sprawling strongholds at the terraced temple-city of Jintha'Alor and the towering Altar of Zul. To the south, the weaker Witherbark tribe clings to Shadra'Alor and Hiri'Watha. The nomadic Revantusk tribe, long scorned by their cousins and lacking a true home, chose a radical path after the Third War: they struck a treaty with Thrall's New Horde. Bolstered by orcish and Forsaken aid, the Revantusk founded Revantusk Village on the eastern sea cliffs, carving out a defiant coastal bastion."],"hash":"a53dc6","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"9e1999bfe3","sec":98},"female-narrator":{"sha":"e0aadc5ee9","sec":103}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Hinterlands","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Hinterlands"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/topic/wildhammer-clan","n":"Wildhammer clan","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/topic/new-horde","n":"New Horde","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/topic/emerald-dream","n":"Emerald Dream","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/topic/troll","n":"Troll","k":"topic"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/durnholde-keep","n":"Durnholde Keep","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/arathi","n":"Arathi Highlands","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/hillsbrad","n":"Hillsbrad Foothills","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/westernplaguelands","n":"Western Plaguelands","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/twilight-grove","n":"Twilight Grove","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/grim-batol","n":"Grim Batol","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/quest/626-cortellos-riddle","n":"Cortello's Riddle","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/3821-dreadmaul-rock","n":"Dreadmaul Rock","k":"quest"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/quest/77-a-sticky-situation","n":"A Sticky Situation","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/7842-another-message-to-the-wildhammer","n":"Another Message to the Wildhammer","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/7830-avenging-the-fallen","n":"Avenging the Fallen","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/7844-cannibalistic-cousins","n":"Cannibalistic Cousins","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/2935-consult-master-gadrin","n":"Consult Master Gadrin","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/7850-dark-vessels","n":"Dark Vessels","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/485-find-oox-09-hl","n":"Find OOX-09/HL!","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/7816-gammerita-mon","n":"Gammerita, Mon!","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/2932-grim-message","n":"Grim Message","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/quest/1450-gryphon-master-talonaxe","n":"Gryphon Master T